    "content": "Upward Bound is a federally funded TRIO program that provides free college preparatory support to high school students from low-income backgrounds and families where parents did not complete a bachelor's degree. It helps participants succeed in high school and enroll in college through tutoring, mentoring, career counseling, and summer residential programs. Key Aspects of Upward Bound: Target Audience: High school students (typically 9-12th grade) who are potential first-generation college students or meet low-income criteria. Services Provided: Free tutoring, SAT/ACT prep, academic advising, college application assistance, financial aid (FAFSA) guidance, and cultural field trips. Structure: Operates year-round with after-school sessions during the academic year and a 6-week intensive summer program, often held on college campuses. Goal: To increase the rates at which participants enroll in and graduate from institutions of postsecondary education. Programs: Includes standard Upward Bound, Upward Bound Math & Science (UBMS), and Veterans Upward Bound. The program is funded by the U.S. Department of Education and has been in operation since the 1960s as part of the War on Poverty programs.",
